1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,640
一台一米八的机器人空翻落地，
A 1.8-meter robot lands a flip,

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:04,090
一条腿飞了出去。
and one of its legs flies off.

3
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:05,390
腿说：我先走了。
The leg: I'm out.

4
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:06,820
机器人：等等我！
The robot: wait for me!

5
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:09,390
这是10月22日，宇树H2-X
This was Unitree's H2-X on October 22,

6
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:11,390
在自家发布会上的表演。
live at the company's own launch event.

7
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:13,760
今天的问题：机器人那么硬，
Today's question: robots are so tough,

8
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,340
腿怎么说掉就掉？
so how does a leg just fall off?

9
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:16,580
认识一下小翻，
Meet Flip,

10
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:18,830
一个热爱空翻的小机器人。
a little robot who loves flips.

11
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:21,670
据报道，H2-X身高大约1米82，
Reportedly, the H2-X is about 1.82 meters tall

12
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:23,290
体重大约70公斤。
and weighs about 70 kilos.

13
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:25,870
宣传片里，它从4米高台翻下来，
In its promo video, it flips off a 4-meter platform

14
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:26,860
稳稳落地。
and sticks the landing.

15
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,790
可现场这一次，侧空翻转到一半，
But live on stage, halfway through a side flip,

16
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:30,890
姿态乱了。
it lost its balance.

17
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:34,080
落地没站稳，右边小腿从关节处脱落，
It landed badly, and the right lower leg came off at the joint

18
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,510
滑到了垫子上。
and slid across the mat.

19
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:37,360
第一个道理：一跳起来，
Lesson one: once you leave the ground,

20
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:38,660
转多少就定了。
your spin is locked in.

21
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,590
空中没有东西可以推，
There's nothing to push on in midair.

22
00:00:40,590 --> 00:00:42,250
这叫角动量守恒。
That's conservation of angular momentum.

23
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,010
就像花样滑冰：手一收转得快，
Like a figure skater: arms in, faster.

24
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:46,510
手一伸转得慢。
Arms out, slower.

25
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:47,600
但总的转动，
But the total spin

26
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,530
起跳那一刻就交了卷。
is handed in at takeoff, like an exam.

27
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:50,840
起跳差一点点，
A tiny error at takeoff

28
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:52,470
落地就歪一大截。
becomes a big tilt at landing.

29
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:55,480
我们估算：侧空翻在空中大约只有半秒，
Our estimate: a side flip is airborne for about half a second.

30
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:57,280
想纠正，几乎来不及。
Barely any time to fix it.

31
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,490
再烧一点：猫从空中掉下，
Even weirder: a falling cat

32
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:01,270
却能在半空翻个身。
can still turn itself over in midair.

33
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:03,880
它先扭前半身、再扭后半身，
It twists its front half, then its back half.

34
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,820
总转动一直是零，照样翻过来。
Total spin stays zero, and it still flips over.

35
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:08,500
机器人也能学这招，
Robots can learn that trick too,

36
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,690
可只有半秒钟，太紧了。
but half a second is tight.

37
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:12,880
第二个道理：落地那一下，
Lesson two: how hard

38
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:13,910
力有多大？
is the landing?

39
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:15,900
我们估算：从半米高落下，
Our estimate: falling half a meter,

40
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,840
落地速度大约每秒3米。
you hit the ground at about 3 meters a second.

41
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:20,920
如果膝盖弯一弯，用30厘米慢慢停，
Bend the knees and stop over 30 centimeters:

42
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:23,390
冲击大约是体重的2.7倍。
the force is about 2.7 times body weight.

43
00:01:23,390 --> 00:01:26,160
如果腿绷直，只用5厘米就停住，
Lock the legs and stop in 5 centimeters:

44
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:28,300
冲击就是体重的11倍！
11 times body weight!

45
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:29,910
70公斤的机器人，
For a 70-kilo robot,

46
00:01:29,910 --> 00:01:32,360
一条腿要扛七百多公斤的力。
one leg takes the force of over 700 kilos.

47
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:34,090
所以人落地都会屈膝，
That's why we bend our knees:

48
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:35,940
时间拉长，力就变小。
stretch the time, shrink the force.

49
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:37,830
人跑步时，每一步脚下，
When you run, each step pushes on the ground

50
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:39,670
大约是体重的两三倍。
with about two to three times your weight.

51
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:41,030
体操运动员落地，
Gymnasts land with knees, ankles and hips

52
00:01:41,030 --> 00:01:43,530
膝盖、脚踝、髋部一起当弹簧。
all working as springs.

53
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:45,550
第三个道理，最反直觉：
Lesson three, the weirdest:

54
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:47,130
腿不怕压，怕掰。
legs don't mind squeezing. They hate bending.

55
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:49,810
就像一根筷子：顺着压很难压断，
Like a chopstick: push along it, it holds.

56
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:51,180
横着一掰就断。
Bend it sideways, snap.

57
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:53,960
我们推测：姿态一歪，力从侧面来，
Our guess: with the body tilted, the force comes sideways,

58
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:56,340
整条腿就成了被横掰的筷子。
and the leg becomes a bent chopstick.

59
00:01:56,340 --> 00:01:57,800
而最先吃不住的，
And the first thing to give

60
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,750
往往是关节这种接缝。
is usually a seam, like a joint.

61
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:03,080
据报道，它腿部关节扭矩大约360牛米，
Reportedly its leg joints make about 360 newton-meters,

62
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:04,600
能一脚踢开车门。
enough to kick in a car door.

63
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,360
可力气大不等于扛得住：
But strong isn't the same as tough:

64
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,240
齿轮、螺栓，都有极限。
gears and bolts all have limits.

65
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:10,540
机器人腿里，电机就是肌肉，
In a robot leg, the motors are the muscles.

66
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:12,970
落地时要像弹簧一样往回收。
On landing they have to give, like springs.

67
00:02:12,970 --> 00:02:14,970
要是这一刻控制没算准，
If the control gets that moment wrong,

68
00:02:14,970 --> 00:02:16,370
电机就会硬顶。
the motors push back stiff.

69
00:02:16,370 --> 00:02:19,370
工程上还有一招：故意留个保险丝，
Engineers also have a trick: a built-in fuse.

70
00:02:19,370 --> 00:02:21,920
先坏便宜的零件，保住贵的。
A cheap part breaks first to save the expensive ones.

71
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:23,910
这次是故障还是保护设计？
Was this a failure, or a safety feature?

72
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:26,180
截至报道，宇树还没有回应。
As of the reports, Unitree hasn't said.

73
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:28,460
友情提示：官方原因还没公布，
Friendly fine print: no official cause yet.

74
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:31,020
今天讲的是我们按物理做的推测。
Today's story is our physics-based guess.

75
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,700
机器人摔一跤不丢人，
A robot falling isn't shameful.

76
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,160
每一跤，工程师都能学到东西。
Every fall teaches the engineers something.

77
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,950
据研究，学走路的小孩，
Studies find toddlers learning to walk

78
00:02:36,950 --> 00:02:38,540
一小时能摔十几次。
fall more than ten times an hour.

79
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:39,880
所以别笑小翻，
So don't laugh at Flip.

80
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,520
它只是在交学费。
It's just paying tuition.

81
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:44,360
下次再空翻，记得：屈膝、站稳，
Next flip, remember: bend, land, stay together.

82
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,660
腿别先走。
Legs, don't leave first.

